:: Help Company Devices [nobr] {"position":"700,4500"}
/* Lists only the devices the player owns ($company.devices, owned), so a device that is still to come stays a surprise */
<p>The strip at the top left shows your <b>devices</b>. Scroll it sideways with the mouse wheel if there are more than fit. Each card has the device's name, a drawing, and its <b>charge</b>: green above 66%, yellow above 33%, red below that.</p>

<<if $company.stage >= 1>>
<h3>Your devices</h3>
<dl class="help-stats">
	<<for _hcdKey, _hcdDevice range $company.devices>>
	<<if _hcdDevice.owned>>
	<dt><<= _hcdDevice.name>></dt><dd><<= _hcdDevice.description>><<if _hcdDevice.calibrationPresets && _hcdDevice.calibrationPresets.length > 0>> Settings: <<= _hcdDevice.calibrationPresets.map(function (k) { return setup.presetLabel(k); }).join(", ")>>.<</if>></dd>
	<</if>>
	<</for>>
</dl>
<p>More devices join the strip as the company builds them.</p>
<</if>>

<h3>The device window</h3>
<p>Click a card to open it:</p>
<ul>
	<li><b>Description</b> of the device.</li>
	<li><b>Calibration</b>: the portrait of $mom.callName or $sister.callName if it is set for one of them, otherwise the name of the setting.</li>
	<li><b>Last used</b>: who it was used on and how many days ago, or "Never used".</li>
	<li><b>Charge</b> as a percentage.</li>
</ul>

<h3>The two buttons</h3>
<dl class="help-stats">
	<dt>Calibrate</dt><dd>Pick a setting from the list and press <b>Calibrate</b> to start the <a href="#" data-help="Help Prototype Minigame">calibration minigame</a>. It costs no time and no charge. If you finish with <b>80% or more</b>, the setting is saved with its quality; below that nothing changes.</dd>
	<dt>Charge</dt><dd>Plugging a device in takes your time, like the early prototype: every action adds <b><<= setup.deviceChargePerAction>>%</b>. <b>Charge</b> spends one action, <b>Charge to full</b> as many as it takes to fill it.</dd>
</dl>
<p>Every night each device you own also regains <b>15%</b> by itself.</p>

<<if $company.stage >= 1>>
<h3>The vent unit</h3>
<p>The last card in the strip is the full-strength $company.prototype.name hidden behind the ceiling vent of the main room. It runs off the building's power, so it has no charge. Instead it has an <b>output level</b>, which you switch in its window. The level sets the target that the company's <a href="#" data-help="Help Company Stats">Efficiency</a> moves toward every night, and how much morale your staff lose while they work:</p>
<table class="help-table">
	<tr><th>Level</th><th>Output</th><th>Efficiency target</th><th>Morale cost of work</th></tr>
	<<for _hcdLevel range setup.ventLevels>>
	<tr><td><<= _hcdLevel.name>><<if _hcdLevel === setup.ventLevel()>> <span class="help-pill">Now</span><</if>></td><td><<= _hcdLevel.output>>%</td><td><<= _hcdLevel.efficiency>></td><td>×<<= _hcdLevel.drain>></td></tr>
	<</for>>
</table>
<p>Off lets them recover. On Low the team loses a little morale over a week, and a weekend or a couple of Coffee Breaks make up for it. Medium gets more done and wears them down over two or three weeks unless the company's Morale is high. High gets the most done for a few days, then they run out of morale by the end of the week and fall behind even Medium, so it's for the week before a deadline; the header reminds you while it is still running there. Efficiency follows the level by <<= setup.companyStatTuning.efficiencyRise>> points per night, so switch a few days early.</p>
<</if>>
<div class="help-note">A finished device doesn't glitch while you calibrate it. Only the unfinished prototype from Stage 0 does.</div>
